{"title":"1988 USAMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/c/86ca6c1c34ee45eabb5363a352de12e1455f8285.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(S)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> assigns to each nine-element subset of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> of the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/f/5ff8e28e952f644ea9ecc9f67e746478f8f7c39e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2,\\ldots, 20\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" /> a whole number from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.  Prove that regardless of how the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is chosen, there will be a ten-element subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/3/e031657b1024dd78b7ef721d668a99d9b9914e21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T\\subset\\{1,2,\\ldots, 20\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/4/5e4623d4f730cc13ed05733beb41adb8c9edf9d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(T - \\{k\\})\\neq k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/0/150aad4eebc645955ac8e906f6613302f5afd4c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\in T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For a given function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />, consider the set of elements <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/3/983ee0dac7fc702b4d15e6049e4feeccacf002ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q \\in P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> paired with elements <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/f/9cf6d4461b12bd13210f943324486ca9ea7c1a05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/b/65b0ad36dc552550fe23bb6c32ffe2e724149be0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(Q) \\ne t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" />. Call the set of pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dccf1268484c07e9565968d3b97605e3ada1824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(Q,t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"20\" /> set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>To employ the Pigeonhole Principle, we need a lower bound on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/9/d69fe9c5d5c49c0e6496b64e7bae9778a68ef149.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lvert R \\rvert$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/e/4ceacb58254ec46b15e34b498c6c0df150ccdc15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{20}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"48\" height=\"55\" /> elements <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa6a4fc8f353522b366f48066da9acd44a4c0cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(Q) \\in Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />, then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> choices for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/b/65b0ad36dc552550fe23bb6c32ffe2e724149be0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(Q) \\ne t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d0780c77ba2840bd268a2b8187709324ea42fa4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(Q) \\notin Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />, then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> choices for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/b/65b0ad36dc552550fe23bb6c32ffe2e724149be0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(Q) \\ne t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/9/7c94e0dfb6a41e166b82a6a188067b9b11c43340.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lvert R \\rvert \\ge 10 \\cdot \\binom{20}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"128\" height=\"55\" />. These pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dccf1268484c07e9565968d3b97605e3ada1824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(Q,t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"20\" /> must be dispersed over all the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-element subsets of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. By the Pigeonhole Principle, some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-element subset of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> must contain at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/6/206774beeed80cf91c8bc088d0a98a79cd9f8c1e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lceil\\frac{\\lvert R \\rvert}{\\binom{20}{10}}\\rceil = \\lceil\\frac{10\\cdot\\binom{20}{9}}{\\binom{20}{10}}\\rceil = \\lceil\\frac{100}{11}\\rceil = 10\\]\" width=\"265\" height=\"49\" /> pairs of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-element subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> with the tenth element <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> of that subset such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/b/65b0ad36dc552550fe23bb6c32ffe2e724149be0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(Q) \\ne t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" />, which satisfies the conditions of the problem.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO\" title=\"1988 USAMO\">1988 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1988 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1988\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1988 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1988 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1988 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1988 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1988 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1988 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017181115\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.031 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.069 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count